    "review_card_3xCdjj": {
      "type": "review-card",
      "blocks": {
        "card_pdp_01": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "my shoulder had been locking up for two years.",
            "body": "My shoulder pain was the worst at night. I could deal with it during the day, but if I rolled onto it in my sleep I’d wake up immediately. I’ve been taking this a little over a month and I’m finally sleeping longer without constantly adjusting pillows. That alone is worth it for me.",
            "name": "Linda R."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_02": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "ran my first 5k since my knee swelled up two years ago",
            "body": "I used to run 4 days a week. Then my right knee swelled up and never fully went back down. Started astaxanthin and the swelling slowly came down over 3 weeks. I ran a full 5k last month. Slow but i finished. I sat in my car after and just sat there for a while. You dont realize what you lost until you get a piece of it back.",
            "name": "David L."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_03": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "menopause took my sleep. Revella gave it back.",
            "body": "my hips burned so bad at night i hadnt slept on my side in over a year. doctor said its just menopause!!! started taking revella and and i began seeing a change within a couple of days - minor but there! I tracked my progress around week 7 i slept on my side through the whole night. thank you revella and team! on my third bag now.",
            "name": "Susan K."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_04": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "6 months post ACL surgery and this is the first thing that actually reduced the swelling",
            "body": "tore my ACL playing basketball. surgery went fine but the inflammation after never fully went away. knee stayed puffy and stiff for months. PT helped with range of motion but the swelling just lingered. my physical therapist mentioned astaxanthin for the anti-inflammatory research. wish i started this day one of recovery - its the only thing that moved the needle enough to give me back mobility.",
            "name": "Marcus T."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_05": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "was skeptical but my shoulder is noticeably better",
            "body": "I got this because my shoulder has been bothering me for a long time, especially at night. I couldn’t sleep on that side and reaching behind me was awful. Im definitely moving better and sleeping with less pain. I already ordered another bottle.",
            "name": "Theresa M."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_06": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "helped with neck stiffness from desk work",
            "body": "I have neck and shoulder tightness from being on the computer all day. I bought this mostly for inflammation. It took a little while, but my neck doesn’t feel as tense at night and I’m sleeping better. I like that it’s easy to take and doesn’t upset my stomach like some other supplements have.",
            "name": "Frank D."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_07": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "my hands were so swollen i couldnt wear my wedding ring.",
            "body": "Perimenopause hit and my fingers blew up. Swollen, stiff, aching. Couldnt wear my wedding ring. Doctor tested me for rheumatoid arthritis — came back negative. Nobody could tell me why. Then I found Revella, started taking it and about  6 weeks in  the swelling went down enough to wear my ring again. It was the minor things for me... but i feel better on it everyday.",
            "name": "Carol A."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_08": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "less achy overall",
            "body": "I’m in my 50s and lately everything has just felt achy — knees, hands, back, shoulders. I didn’t want to keep taking ibuprofen all the time. This took about 3-4 weeks before I really noticed anything, but I do feel less stiff overall. The biggest difference is getting up in the morning. I don’t feel 25 again, but I feel better.",
            "name": "Gloria S."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_09": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "i reorganized my entire kitchen around my shoulder pain.",
            "body": "plates in the bottom drawer. cereal where the pots used to go. i moved everything to waist level so i would never have to reach up. ordered Revella because i had nothing left to try. week 2 the morning stiffness was gone. week 4 i put the coffee back where it belongs. my husband noticed and asked what changed. Revella changed!",
            "name": "Nancy K."
          }
        },
        "card_pdp_10": {
          "type": "card",
          "settings": {
            "rating": 5,
            "star_color_filled": "#e8a020",
            "star_color_empty": "#dddddd",
            "heading": "i stopped waking up with a yelp every time i rolled over",
            "body": "I would be up nightly, don't think I would sleep for more than 1 hour at a time unless i forced myself with pillows to stay on my back... heating pads, ibuprofen, nothing helped like Revella did. It was not just the sleep quality and pain that went away during the night, but the daily mobility i regained. I just felt looser after about a month of taking it - can't really put it any other way.",
            "name": "Patricia H."
