        "review_group_QqgX4N": {
          "type": "review_group",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "name_1": "Todd L.",
            "rating_1": 5,
            "text_1": "bad knees from running for 20 years. 10 weeks in and the daily ache is noticeably less. i started running again twice a week. my orthopedic said whatever youre doing keep doing it because the inflammation markers in my blood dropped.",
            "image_url_1": "",
            "name_2": "Cheryl N.",
            "rating_2": 5,
            "text_2": "both hips. both knees. menopause hit and my lower body just fell apart. i went from hiking on weekends to barely making it through a grocery store. 8 weeks later i did a short hike with my daughter. she cried. i cried. first time in 2 years.",
            "image_url_2": "",
            "name_3": "Jean M.",
            "rating_3": 5,
            "text_3": "my doctor said the shoulder will unfreeze on its own in 1-2 years. i said i cant wait 2 years i have a life to live. i am at about 90% range of motion at month 4. my doctor said some people just heal faster. i didnt tell him about the supplement.",
            "image_url_3": "",
            "name_4": "Rick H.",
            "rating_4": 5,
            "text_4": "construction worker. 52 years old. knees shoulders lower back — all inflamed all the time. by month 2 the baseline inflammation just dropped. the constant burning background pain is gone. thats the difference between functioning and suffering.",
            "image_url_4": "",
            "name_5": "Judith A.",
            "rating_5": 5,
            "text_5": "I am 61 and postmenopausal. my friend had been on this for 3 months and looked like a different person. she moved differently. 7 weeks in and i understand now. the inflammation just quiets down. thats the only way i can describe it.",
            "image_url_5": ""
          }
        },
        "review_group_6TJfcy": {
          "type": "review_group",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "name_1": "Carolyn E.",
            "rating_1": 5,
            "text_1": "menopause took my flexibility. i used to do yoga 4 times a week. by week 6 i was back on the mat. by week 12 i was almost back to my normal practice. i lost a year of my life to that inflammation and im angry nobody told me sooner.",
            "image_url_1": "",
            "name_2": "Virginia R.",
            "rating_2": 5,
            "text_2": "i bought every joint supplement on amazon over 2 years. spent hundreds. this helped a lot. the difference is it goes somewhere the others physically cannot. i wish id found it first and saved myself 2 years.",
            "image_url_2": "",
            "name_3": "Joe P.",
            "rating_3": 5,
            "text_3": "my wife ordered this for me because she was tired of hearing me complain about my knees. week 5 i realized i hadnt complained in a while. she pointed that out too. she doesnt need to know she was right though.",
            "image_url_3": "",
            "name_4": "Ruth S.",
            "rating_4": 5,
            "text_4": "54 and my hands swelled up so bad i had to cut my wedding ring off. that was the lowest point. 8 weeks in the swelling is controlled. not wearing my ring yet but my fingers are close.",
            "image_url_4": "",
            "name_5": "Beverly H.",
            "rating_5": 5,
            "text_5": "i almost gave up at week 3 because nothing felt different. so glad i didnt. week 5 is when the shift happened. by week 8 i was up and moving within 15 minutes of waking up. if youre reading this and thinking about quitting early — dont.",
            "image_url_5": ""
          }
        },
        "review_group_FFMpiX": {
          "type": "review_group",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "name_1": "Paul D.",
            "rating_1": 5,
            "text_1": "herniated disc plus knee arthritis plus shoulder impingement. added this and the background inflammation dropped enough that i could cut the NSAIDs in half. my liver enzymes improved at my next blood test too. doctor was pleased but wouldnt credit the supplement. thats fine. i know.",
            "image_url_1": "",
            "name_2": "Janice H.",
            "rating_2": 5,
            "text_2": "i work as a hairdresser. standing all day, arms overhead for 8 hours. the shoulder pain from menopause was threatening my career. by week 6 i was making it through a full day without the burning. im 58 and i wasnt ready to retire. this kept me working.",
            "image_url_2": "",
            "name_3": "Evelyn W.",
            "rating_3": 5,
            "text_3": "finishing bag 2 now. the joint pain from menopause is about 70% better. hips dont burn at night. knees dont lock on the stairs. the improvement was gradual enough that i didnt notice until i realized i stopped reaching for the ibuprofen bottle.",
            "image_url_3": "",
            "name_4": "Brent T.",
            "rating_4": 5,
            "text_4": "i read the actual studies before ordering. astaxanthin at 12mg has peer reviewed clinical data for inflammation and joint function. results matched the literature. joint pain reduced measurably by week 6. the evidence base is solid and my knees agree.",
            "image_url_4": "",
            "name_5": "Norma J.",
            "rating_5": 5,
            "text_5": "this is my third bag. the last time i ran low i stretched it out to every other day and within a week my hips started aching again. every single day. no skipping.",
            "image_url_5": ""
          }
